Pako Engineers - Standard Tolerances Guide

General machining tolerances are controlled by customer drawing, approved QAP, and applicable ISO/DIN/ASME standards.

Typical achievable values:
- Turned diameters: down to 0.005 mm where geometry permits
- Ground bearing fits: Ra 0.2 to 0.8 microns
- Face runout: 0.01 mm to 0.02 mm depending on diameter
- Shaft straightness: 0.05 mm per meter
- Keyways and slots: inspected by calibrated gauges or CMM

All dimensions remain subject to drawing review and manufacturability confirmation.
